    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d529-a6">

                <pb facs="0731" n="637" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg637"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 517.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hyatt to Mr.
                            Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago de Cuba</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-05-16"><hi rendition="#italic">May 16,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 257.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to herewith inclose for
                    your information further correspondence relative to the arrest and imprisonment
                    of Bert S. Skiller, referred to in my dispatch No. 240, of April 10, who still
                    remains in the prison of this city under marine jurisdiction.</p>
                <p>It will be seen by the correspondence inclosed that a speedy transfer to civil
                    jurisdiction is promised.</p>
                <p>It is a matter of grave concern that under the present administration of affairs
                    on this island the protocol of May 12, 1877, between Spain and the United States
                    is ineffectual in securing speedy justice to American citizens.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pulaski F. Hyatt</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
